author ai
group gui
note How the panels around the centre are placed, resized and moved. Three panels (Paths/Symbols/Files, Xrefs, Output) each sit on one edge of the window - left, right or bottom - in an order along that edge and at a size across it. The layout is one list of places in the Model's Dock, read every frame: the view asks for every size first, clamped so the centre stays usable, then draws each edge's panels in list order with a splitter on the centre side. Dragging a splitter puts the panel's inner edge under the pointer; pressing a panel's header and dragging shows a band where it would land and moves it there on release. The pointer is read before the tree is built and turned into dock actions that are applied at once, so the frame that sees a drag already draws it. Nothing is saved: a launch starts from the default layout.

