note Called by the frame right after the element tree begins, before any size is read, and its actions are applied at once, so a drag shows in the frame it happens and a click after a drop is hit-tested against the new layout. A held splitter becomes a Resize that puts its panel's inner edge under the pointer, from last frame's rectangle of the panel, so the edge follows the pointer with no drift from summing per-frame deltas. A held header is dragged; released, it becomes a Release carrying the drop target if the grab had started moving, and none otherwise.

